      "extract": "It is accurate to state that one of the most important developments in probability theory in the last century was Stein's method. Stein's method is a highly original technique and has been useful in proving normal and Poisson approximation theorems in probability problems with limited information such as the knowledge of only a few moments of the random variable. Stein's method can be difficult to work with and",
